msgstr "Keycord d amsaɣ udlif amsasa i yikaramen n wawalen n uεeddi iseqdacen tuddsa tamagnut n pass. Ikufan yellan qqimen d ikufan pass imagnuten ɣef uḍebsi, ihi mazal tteddun akked pass d yifecka-nniḍen imṣadanen."

#: src/composition/host_access.rs:64
msgid "Keycord is running in a protected space, so some optional features stay off until you allow this. If you allow it, Keycord can use tools from your computer such as GPG, the Host backend, and pass import. If you don't, Keycord still works with the integrated backend."
msgstr "Keycord iteddu deg tallunt iwgelhen; akka, kra n timahilin tifrananin qqiment nsant alamma tsirgeḍ aya. Ma tsirgeḍ-t, Keycord yezmer ad iseqdec ifecka n uselkim-ik·im am GPG, backend Asezdeɣ d pass import. Ma ur tsirgeḍ ara, Keycord ad ikemmel ad yeddu s backend Yeddan."

#: crates/keycord-passkey/src/ui.rs:125
msgid "Keycord opened a credential export request that names {importer} as the importer and checked its structure. The local file does not authenticate that identity. Keycord does not yet generate CXP response archives, so no passkey data was released."
msgstr "Keycord yeldi asuter n usifeḍ n yinekcumen i d-yebdren {importer} d amaktar, yerna isenqed tameẓka-ines. Afaylu adigan ur isestebbat ara tamagit-a. Keycord ur d-yesnulfuy ara akka tura iɣbaren n tririt CXP; ulac isefka n tsarut n uεeddi i d-yettwasuffɣen."

#: crates/keycord-preferences/src/ui/settings.rs:288
msgid "Keycord will first make its private-key list match the GPG private keys on your computer. After that, creating, importing, or deleting a private key in Keycord will update the host too. Keys that only exist in Keycord may be removed during the first sync."
msgstr "Uqbel, Keycord ad yerr tabdart-ines n tsura tusligin temṣada d tsura GPG tusligin n uselkim-ik·im. Seld waya, mi ara d-tesirweḍ, ad tketreḍ neɣ ad tekkseḍ tasarut tusligt deg Keycord, asezdeɣ ad yettwaleqqem daɣen. Tisura i yellan kan deg Keycord zemrent ad ttwakksent deg umtawi amezwaru."

